  "source": {
    "plan": "Callboard row 2026-12-01 (storyhowto, nobody-brings, Canberk's priority 1 tier list), the earliest planned row on 2026-11-26; look collage",
    "project": "ppvqmbzuqvzpiuqaiqfy",
    "sql": "select m.id, m.character_name, m.estimated_duration_seconds, m.overdone_score, p.title, p.author, p.copyright_status from monologues m join plays p on p.id=m.play_id where m.id = 32446 or (p.author ilike '%Shakespeare%' and (m.text ilike 'Gallop apace%' or m.text ilike 'To be, or not to be%' or m.text ilike '%Hath not a Jew eyes%'))",
    "checked": "2026-11-26: 32446 Isabella (The White Devil, John Webster, play 2914, public domain) 71s = 1:11, overdone 0, opens 'O that I were a man, or that I had power To execute my apprehended wishes!'. In the library too: Juliet 'Gallop apace' (67, overdone 0.85), Hamlet 'To be, or not to be' (12213, overdone 1), Shylock's 'Hath not a Jew eyes' speech (1358, overdone 0.9); they appear only as named cards with their first words",
    "changed_from_plan": "the row's search ('a revenge monologue for a woman, under two minutes, not Shakespeare') returns The Duchess (The Duchess of Malfi), Tamora and Lady Macbeth first and Isabella 24th; the row's fallback 'Isabella White Devil' returns Lodovico and Flamineo first. 'a woman who wishes she were a man so she could take revenge' returns Isabella first with BEST PICK, so the film types that and the voice says 'asked for a woman who wants revenge'. The stage door queue and the scarf are one beat. Total 27.05s",
    "app": "Ghost Light web preview built from actorrise main apps/mobile (fd0697e1) plus web-preview.patch (applied with git apply; serve.sh's clone of the archived ghostlight repo no longer takes the patch), dark theme, demo account, 2026-11-26",
    "flow": "flows/search-tier-list.json (shots -> public/story/2026-12-01-tier-list/*.png; Tonight's speech line blurred on search and typed)",
    "voice": "George, one take at stability 0.5, Scribe 0.98, sped up 1.38x with fit_take.py; AI voice, labelled on every platform",
    "new_scene_types": "tier (cut-paper collage) with four beats: hook, door, cards, top. New collage pieces: TBoard (the S to F board), TCardPiece (ranked cards), TRain, the stage door with its lamp and sign, the muttering queue, the x6 tally, the 1:11 tag, confetti",
    "motifs": "tier-board,ranked-paper-cards,stage-door-in-the-rain,scarf-shut-in-the-door,muttering-queue,x6-tally,confetti-on-S",
    "end": "specs/2026-12-01-tier-list-end.json, joined with scripts/join.sh",
